    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/explore-careers/applicant-information/": {
      "title": "Teaching areas",
      "description": "Applicant Information - Future Staff Skip to main content menu Menu settings Quick links search Search Apply Now EOI Current students Campus map Contact us close Close quick links Search Search close Close search Future Staff Home Discover Curtin Why Work at Curtin Diversity Equity and Inclusion at Curtin Popular Links Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Employment Why work at Curtin Applicant Information Current Opportunities Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Employment Living and Working in Western Australia Explore Careers Applicant Information Apply Now Future Staff Home Explore Careers Applicant Information Applicant Information Applicant Information Curtin welcomes applications from domestic and international applicants for all available opportunities. Explore the application process and discover what we’re looking for in our applicants. Application Preparation The application process What's next? Application Preparation Correctly preparing your application gives you the best chance at being shortlisted for interview. Your application should includes sufficient information about your suitability for the position and demonstrate how your skills, knowledge and experience match with the requirements of the role. The application process To begin, visit our Job board and browse all available opportunities. You can use the filters at the top of the page to define the roles best suited to you. If you are interested in an opportunity, select the ‘Apply Now’ icon. You will need to fill in the relevant information to be considered for the position. Please ensure your email address is entered correctly as this will be the main contact. Remember to attach your Curriculum Vitae and any other necessary documentation (such as the Equivalency of Qualification Criteria and Evidence ) to be considered for the position. Take time to read the declaration and tick the check box to agree to it, then click the ‘Submit Application’ button when you are ready. What's next? An automatic reply will be sent to your email address, confirming acceptance of your application. Your application will then be assessed and considered. If you are shortlisted, you will be invited to an interview. Employment Conditions We value the contribution of our employees by offering a range of employment conditions and generous salaries. Enterprise Agreements Learn more about the employment conditions at Curtin University Curtin Academic, Professional and General staff members Curtin Sport and Recreation Curtin Early Learning Centre Salary Scales View our current salary rates for the following types of employment Academic staff Casual academic staff Curtin English academic staff General/professional staff (individual) General/professional staff (joint) Childcare staff Current opportunities View the current employment opportunities available for academic and professional employees. Apply Now Current Opportunities View the current employment opportunities available for academic and professional employees. Apply Now Expressions of Interest Complete the EOI form to be kept on our candidate database and receive notifications of relevant roles that match your skills. *Please note the form is not an application and all applications still need to be completed for specific roles. EOI SUBMISSION Related links Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Employment Why Work at Curtin Diversity, Inclusion and Beloning About us Information for... Future students Current students Current staff Future staff Alumni Visitors Parents Community partners Industry partners Media Quick links Student Oasis Staff Portal Library Learning & Teaching Staff Directory Giving to Curtin Contact us Teaching areas Centre for Aboriginal Studies Business and Law Health Sciences Humanities Science and Engineering Campuses Perth Kalgoorlie Dubai Malaysia Mauritius Singapore Address Kent Street, Bentley, Perth, Western Australia 6102 Postal address GPO Box U1987, Perth WA 6845 Telephone +61 8 9266 9266 Follow Curtin Twitter Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn CRICOS Provider Code: 00301J ABN: 99 143 842 569 TEQSA: PRV12158 Copyright Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Contact Curtin University would like to pay our respect to the indigenous members of our community by acknowledging the traditional owners of the land on which the Perth campus is located, the Wadjuk people of the Nyungar Nation; and on our Kalgoorlie campus, the Wongutha people of the North-Eastern Goldfields."
